Subject: [PATCH vstorage] Push nested subcomponents onto the component stack
Message-ID: <178929518181.17287.11968853769603087037-0@git.sr.ht>
X-Mailer: git.sr.ht
Reply-to: ~randogoth <kflux@posteo.de>
To: ~whynothugo/vdirsyncer-devel@lists.sr.ht
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
MIME-Version: 1.0

From: randogoth <kflux@posteo.de>

ItemBuilder::push_subcomponent() appended the new subcomponent straight
into the parent's subcomponents list instead of pushing it onto
component_stack. pop_subcomponent() (called on the matching END: line)
still pops component_stack unconditionally, so the first nested
component (e.g. a VALARM inside a VEVENT) empties the stack on its
END: line, and the next current() call panics with "component_stack
non-empty".

This affects any VEVENT/VTODO/VJOURNAL containing a nested
sub-component parsed via Component::parse_split, which is used by
WebCalStorage::list_items to split a feed into individual items. In
practice this reliably crashes pimsync when syncing any webcal feed
containing an alarm.
---
 src/simple_component.rs | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/simple_component.rs b/src/simple_component.rs
index 7a4d6cc..8b0bdb9 100644
--- a/src/simple_component.rs
+++ b/src/simple_component.rs
@@ -294,7 +294,7 @@ impl<'a> ItemBuilder<'a> {
     }

     fn push_subcomponent(&mut self, component: Component<'a>) {
-        self.current().subcomponents.push(component);
+        self.component_stack.push(component);
     }

     fn pop_subcomponent(&mut self) {
@@ -631,4 +631,25 @@ mod test {
             Err(ComponentError::DataAfterEnd)
         );
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn test_event_with_valarm() {
+        use super::Component;
+
+        let calendar = [
+            "BEGIN:VCALENDAR",
+            "BEGIN:VEVENT",
+            "UID:test-event",
+            "BEGIN:VALARM",
+            "ACTION:DISPLAY",
+            "TRIGGER:-PT15M",
+            "END:VALARM",
+            "END:VEVENT",
+            "END:VCALENDAR",
+        ]
+        .join("\r\n");
+
+        let components = Component::parse_split(&calendar).unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(components.len(), 1);
+    }
 }
